Package: mynah
Version: @VERSION@
Section: utils
Priority: optional
Architecture: @ARCH@
Depends: @DEPENDS@
Recommends: pipewire-bin, wl-clipboard
Maintainer: Matthew Hagrelius <matthew@hagreli.us>
Homepage: https://github.com/mhagrelius/mynah
Description: Dictation for the GNOME desktop
 Mynah puts a global shortcut on your keyboard: press it, say what you
 mean, press it again, and the words appear in whatever window you were
 already working in.
 .
 Speech recognition runs on your own machine using NVIDIA's Parakeet
 models, so nothing you dictate leaves it. A vocabulary you control
 fixes the names and jargon the model mishears, spoken numbers are
 written as digits, and an optional pass through a local language model
 takes out the "um"s.
